r#  5142  77  70
p: .
t. 
|  Not only are their opinions given great weight in evaluations of abuse
|  charges - in some cases, their role extends even beyond the evaluative
|  stage. For example, they can act as court-appointed visitation
|  supervisors (supervising a mother’s visits with her children)
|  and as court-appointed
|  family counselors, even after the litigation is over. They can also
|  serve as consultants to Child Protective Services (CPS), which means
|  that they can recommend that charges be filed against a mother they
|  deem paranoid or delusional. These various roles multiply the effect
.  of the theories that such experts carry into each particular case


--- Sentence/switch
