p: .
t. 
|  But if she is simply mistaken in her suspicions, no penalty may be
|  legally applied to her. We have previously mentioned (see Chapter 4,
|  note 15) a New Jersey appellate court that ruled a family court cannot
|  punish a mother for her subjective beliefs about a child’s sexual abuse,
|  even if the court does not ultimately endorse them. This ruling reflects
.  fundamental legal principles

--- Sentence/end 
