p: .
t. 
|  But this, of course, assumes that beliefs are not automatically translated into action. That is, a woman who knows her belief that sexual
|  abuse has occurred was not ratified by a court can refrain from alienating
|  the child from the father once she knows she is legally forbidden to do
|  so. This is the assumption the law makes of all ordinary people. It must
|  do so; otherwise, a great many people could be treated as guilty until
.  proved innocent

--- Sentence/end 
id: 115
r#  59803  911  17

--- Paragraph/end 
