|  The next case narrative describes the case of a Brooklyn mother who
|  lost sole custody of her six-year-old son because a mental health expert, chosen by the father, invoked a permutation of PAS, declaring
|  there was a danger to the child because of the mother’s display of resist and refuse dynamics with [the child] toward his father.\127 When
|  asked in court to clarify this concept, the expert stated: It’s many people
|  who work in the divorce and forensic area [that] are preferring this
|  term [resist and refuse dynamics] to, and basically has similar meaning to, parental alienation but it’s being preferred because it’s more
|  descriptive ...\ and doesn’t imply a presumption of what the cause
|  of the problem is. The expert immediately went on to assert that the
|  child was showing what I call embryonic or early signs of attitudes
|  and statements that are more intensified resist and refuse dynamics to
|  come.\128So, although similar to PAS pseudoscience, this permutation,
|  Resist and Refuse Dynamics (R-RD),
|  has the added dimension of an extraordinary prognostic capability of
|  detecting from the very early signs of R-RD how such dynamics will pick
|  up steam over time. Armed with a crystal ball, the expert can supposedly
|  tell, from the very early signs of parental alienation, what will happen
.  in the relatively distant future

--- Sentence/end 
