|  As it turned out, the investigators for the New York City Administration for Children’s Services (ACS) found nothing of the kind. They
|  spoke to the mother’s therapist, who confirmed that the mother had no
|  mental illness history and had not even been prescribed psychotropic
|  medication. Instead, she sought episodic counseling due to a prior life
|  traumatic situation and is deemed stable - and not in need of frequent therapy sessions because of her demonstration of progress.\135
|  Yet, the bogus mental illness labels that had been ascribed to the mother
|  during her family court litigation (i.e., a purported personality disorder) allowed her ex-partner to discredit her. On the other hand, the
